{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "purpose": "simulation Phase 2 (#841): sm.predict(complist=...) scenarios run by CASA and by casa-rs",
  "notes": [
    "The oracle writes each of 'complists' with CASA's cl tool under <out>/complists/ before the scenarios run (each entry is one cl.addcomponent's keyword arguments, 'dir' as [frame, longitude, latitude]); CASA reads a list read-only, so casa-rs reads the same table.",
    "Image models are named relative to the oracle's --model-root, as in sm_predict_scenarios.json (alma/ is 256 pixels of 0.05 arcsec centred on 10h -30d, alma-big/ 512 of 0.15 arcsec centred on (0.0007615435494667714, -0.0001523087098933758) rad).",
    "Two CASA defects are kept out of these scenarios, as casa-rs does not follow them (docs/CASA (C++) bugs.md): a negative flux under the beam, which CASA's full-spectral beam turns positive, and a polarised component with a single spectral index, whose Stokes indices CASA's matrix sampler reads out of bounds.",
    "Times and the configuration keep every scenario free of shadowing and elevation flags.",
    "The moved-pointing scenarios observe a second pointing of 'target' that observemany moves 10.4 arcsec east, keeping target's FIELD row (#884): CASA phases its rows on the field, from FIELD's PHASE_DIR, and centres the beam on POINTING's direction, where the antennas point. at-moved.cl's point sits there, where ALMA's 230 GHz beam centred on the field is about 0.6 of its peak."
  ],
